WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.455
- It is time for Drew's News,

00:00:02.455 --> 00:00:06.154
your daily sighting of the
majestic good news whale.

00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:07.800
(mimics water whooshing)

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.710
Right out the blowhole.
- Was that your blowhole?

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.440
- Yeah. (laughs)
- Oh yeah, I figured it out.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.100
- It was.
- Okay. I got it.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.960
- Well, with me at the
desk is the best co-pilot

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:16.870
in the business,

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.725
Ross "Your Awesome" Matthews.
- Hi, everybody. Hi!

00:00:19.725 --> 00:00:22.319
(audience applauds)
Blowhole.

00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:25.029
(mimicking water whooshing)

00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:30.029
- First up today in the
headlines, she is a culinary icon.

00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:32.670
- Mm hmm.
- Julia Child is back.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.600
- Julia!
- Oh yes!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.567
And Food &amp; Wine reports that
the Food Network is launching

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.820
"The Julia Child Challenge,"

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.930
which is the competition show where chefs

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.630
will recreate Julia's classic recipes.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.190
It's literally gonna
be like a side by side

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.330
and it's all for a chance for the prize

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.260
to go to a French cooking school.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.203
Take a look.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.120
- [Voiceover] They'll
cook alongside their hero.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.630
- Mm, this really yummy.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.010
- [Voiceover] Who also
started as a home cook.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.730
- I just love to muck
around in the kitchen.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.850
- [Voiceover] And found
her calling later in life.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:05.487
- Welcome to "The French Chef."

00:01:05.487 --> 00:01:06.560
I'm Julia Child.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.040
- [Voiceover] They'll cook
in a kitchen, just like hers.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.770
- It's so close to the real thing

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.160
- [Voiceover] With the same
ingredients that she used

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.520
that made her.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.783
- Voila!
- Julia.

00:01:16.783 --> 00:01:18.727
- Sill alive.
- Uh huh.

00:01:18.727 --> 00:01:20.953
(audience cheers)

00:01:20.953 --> 00:01:23.980
I mean, if this isn't appointment TV,

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.170
I don't know what is.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:28.420
It starts tonight on the
Food Network, but wait,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.770
there's more if you need it,

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.867
because HBO Max is launching
their own scripted series,

00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:36.560
"Julia," about the
visionary leap that she took

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.100
onto television in 1963.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.320
And it's starring Sarah Lancashire

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.053
and David Hyde Pierce as
Julia's husband, Paul.

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:48.760
Ross.
- I know

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.130
- I can't.
- I can, I'll tell you.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.960
I love Julia Child,
Julia, for many reasons

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.888
but there's something about Julia.

00:01:56.888 --> 00:01:58.670
She made you feel like you
could embrace the mistakes

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.560
in the kitchen and hello.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.010
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.590
Rebel homemaker.
- I mean, I am a human,

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.360
living, walking, breathing mistake.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.732
- Yeah. (laughs)
- Just.

00:02:07.732 --> 00:02:11.180
You know, I am! I'm all
about the messing up.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.070
- Also, there's something
about her I relate to.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.840
I mean, she sounded different.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.650
She looked different than
everybody else on television.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:20.790
And that's why we fell in love with her.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:21.780
And there should be more people

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.654
that don't fit the mold television.

00:02:24.654 --> 00:02:27.990
(audience applauds)
I love that about her.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.320
- You're so right, Rossy.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.060
One time I had breakfast
with Meryl Streep.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.790
I swear this is a true story.
- Hold on.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:37.320
I'm gonna need CPR real
quick. Anyone wanna?

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.430
- I know, and she, I got there
and she was already there.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.720
I was like, "Of course,
Meryl beat me there.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.680
Oh, I should have been waiting
for her, it's Meryl Streep."

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.380
And I came in and she had her script open

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.170
and she was like, "Yeah, I'm just doing,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:53.167
learning this dialect for my
next character, Julia Child."

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.160
And I was like, "I think
it's gonna be amazing."

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.220
- [Ross] Yeah, and she
was nominated for an Oscar

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.920
for it.
_ If that isn't, like,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.630
the go-to movie when it
comes across your scroll

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.360
of your TV guide.
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.680
- Every time I will dip in.
- I can't go past it,

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.513
no matter what,

00:03:10.513 --> 00:03:11.750
I have to watch it.
- "Julia and Julia."

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.830
It's the greatest movie.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.370
Amy Adams, Stanley Tucci,

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.820
So Julia for everything

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.250
- Well Meryl, you were
amazing in "Julia and Julia."

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.569
We can't wait for all this
Julia Child love coming up.

00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:24.236
(upbeat music)

